  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nThe pattern continues to shift going into Thursday with a large\nscale trough deepening across western CONUS. Within the flow of\nthis large scale trough a smaller weather system will push across\nMexico and eject into the southern plains. In doing so this system\nwill draw up moisture into the panhandles starting on Thursday.\nThe moisture coupled with the weather system will bring about the\nnext round of rain showers and thunderstorms for the panhandles.\nThe weather system is most likely to reach its peak late on\nThursday through Friday morning. Just as fast as it arrived this\nweather system will most likely depart eastward late Friday. This\nwould allow for a small window of calmer weather Saturday into\nearly Sunday. The next weather system has an increasing chance of\nimpacting the southern plains Sunday into Monday bringing a\nfurther round of rain showers and thunderstorms. This period of\nactive weather will also more likely than not lead to a drop in\nthe temperatures. However, there doesn't seem to be any pushes of\ncold air so even with a drop in the temperatures it will most\nlikely still remain above normal. So we are still waiting on the\nfirst snow of the season.",
